      "short": "$\\frac{10}{15}$, as it is larger than $\\frac{3}{5}$. Correct answer: d.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{5}&=\\frac{3\\times3}{5\\times3}=\\frac{9}{15}\\\\\\frac{10}{15}&>\\frac{9}{15}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\frac{10}{15}$ is larger than the upper bound $\\frac{3}{5}$ and cannot lie between the marked fractions. Correct answer: d.",
